use std
into render.amni

Imports: os, web, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.envmap and gfx.scene3d. This is Amni-CAD's Helium render view. It draws a model on the page's canvas; the page writes the settings and the pose of everything that moves into shared buffers and everything is applied inside `he_frame`.

Globals: `C f32[40]` (camera and look settings, written every frame), `L f32[16]` (lighting, written when it changes), `var asset = -1`, `var item = -1`, `var ground_item = -1`, `var sw = 0`, `var sh = 0`, `var iw = 0`, `var ih = 0`, `var light f32 = 0.0`, `var P f32[>..] = []` (the pose of moving nodes and lights, written every frame), `var padded = false`.

Declare `extern fn hv_f32(id i32, xs f32[:]);`.

`main()` sets `gltf::lazy_pixels = true`, and with `a = args()` reads `a[1]` with the unqualified `read_file(a[1], glb)` into a local `var glb byte[>..] = []` (false: print "render: cannot read " plus a[1] and return). `asset = gltf::load_bytes(glb[..], "/m/")` (negative: print "render: " plus `gltf::error()` and return). Read the optional floor with `var gb byte[>..] = []` and `read_file("/m/ground.glb", gb)`; when that is true set `let ga = gltf::load_bytes(gb[..], "/m/")`, and when `ga >= 0`, loop `k` over `gltf::assets[ga].materials.count` and set `gltf::materials[gltf::assets[ga].materials.first + k].no_shadow = true`, so the floor never shades the model. Open the canvas with `gfx::open("amni render", 640, 480)` (false: print "render: " plus `gfx::error()` and return). Only after the canvas has opened, call `hv_f32(0, C[..])` and `hv_f32(1, L[..])`, so the page can tell a failed start from a running view. Then push `0.0` onto `P` `gltf::assets[asset].nodes.count * 15 + 8` times and call `hv_f32(2, P[..])`. `item = s3d::add(asset)`; `s3d::place(item, gfx::mat4_identity)`; when the floor loaded with `ga >= 0`, set `ground_item = s3d::add(ga)` and `s3d::place(ground_item, gfx::mat4_identity)`. Set `s3d::temporal = 1`, `s3d::ao_mode = 1`, `s3d::look.ao_samples = 32`, `s3d::ssr_on = true`, `s3d::ssr_rough = 0.4`, `s3d::spec_occlusion = false`, `s3d::sun = s3d::Sun { to_sun: linalg::unit3(float3 { 0.4, 0.8, 0.45 }), rgb: float3 { 3.0, 3.0, 3.0 }, shadows: true, shadow_far: 10.0, map_size: 2048, angle: 0.02, reach: 1.0, fit: true, contact: 0.02 }`, `s3d::sky = s3d::Sky { zenith: float3 { 0.5, 0.5, 0.5 }, horizon: float3 { 0.5, 0.5, 0.5 }, ground: float3 { 0.5, 0.5, 0.5 }, ambient: 1.0, draw: true }`, `s3d::look.desaturate = 0.0`. Let `z = gfx::screen_size()`; set `sw = z.x as int`, `sh = z.y as int`, `iw = sw`, `ih = sh`; `s3d::init(sw, sh)`; finally call `web::frames(true)` so the page starts calling `he_frame`.

`fn apply_light()`: return when `L[0] == light`. Set `light = L[0]`. Let `to_sun = linalg::unit3(float3 { C[32], C[33], C[34] })`. When `L[1] == 1.0` (daylight sky): call `s3d::atmosphere(to_sun, L[2], L[3], L[4])`, set `envmap::intensity = 1.0` and `s3d::sky.draw = true`. When `L[1] == 2.0` (environment file): when `envmap::load("/m/env.hdr")` is false print "render: cannot read the lighting" and return; set `envmap::intensity = L[2]`, `s3d::sky.draw = L[3] > 0.5`, `s3d::sky.horizon = float3 { L[4], L[5], L[6] }`, `s3d::sun.rgb = float3 { L[7], L[8], L[9] }`.

`fn apply_view()`: set `s3d::view` to an `s3d::Camera` with eye (C[0], C[1], C[2]), target (C[3], C[4], C[5]), up (C[21], C[22], C[23]), fov_y C[6], near C[7], far C[8]. Set `s3d::look.exposure = C[9]`, `s3d::look.curve = C[10] as int`, `s3d::look.bloom = C[11]`, `s3d::look.vignette = C[12]`, `s3d::look.chroma = C[13]`, `s3d::look.grain = C[14]`, `s3d::look.sharpen = C[15]`, `s3d::look.saturation = C[16]`, `s3d::look.contrast = C[17]`, `s3d::look.warmth = C[18]`, `s3d::sun.shadow_far = C[20]`, `s3d::wet = C[24]`, `s3d::snow = C[25]`, `s3d::dof_aperture = C[26]`, `s3d::dof_focus = C[27]`, `envmap::rotation = C[31]`. When `L[1] == 2.0` set `s3d::sun.to_sun = linalg::unit3(float3 { C[32], C[33], C[34] })`. When `ground_item >= 0`, with pivot `p = float3 { C[36], 0.0, C[37] }` and `q = float3 { 0.0 - C[36], 0.0, 0.0 - C[37] }`, call `s3d::place(ground_item, gfx::mul(gfx::translate(p), gfx::mul(gfx::rotate(float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }, C[35]), gfx::translate(q))))`.

`fn apply_pose()`: return when `P.len == 0`. Let `a = gltf::assets[asset]`. When `P[0] > 0.0` and `padded` is false, set `padded = true`, then for each `k` below `a.nodes.count` with `n = gltf::nodes[a.nodes.first + k]`, when `n.mesh >= 0 && n.skin >= 0`, let `m = gltf::meshes[n.mesh]` and for each `q` below `m.prims.count` with `i = m.prims.first + q` set `gltf::prims[i].lo = gltf::prims[i].lo + float3 { P[2], P[3], P[4] }` and `gltf::prims[i].hi = gltf::prims[i].hi + float3 { P[5], P[6], P[7] }`, so shadows cover everywhere a skinned model travels. For each `k` below `P[0] as int`, with `o = 8 + k * 11`, call `s3d::set_node(item, a.nodes.first + P[o] as int, float3 { P[o + 1], P[o + 2], P[o + 3] }, linalg::Quat { x: P[o + 4], y: P[o + 5], z: P[o + 6], w: P[o + 7] }, float3 { P[o + 8], P[o + 9], P[o + 10] })`. Then let `var j = s3d::items[item].light_base` and for each `k` below `P[1] as int`, with `o = 8 + (P[0] as int) * 11 + k * 4`: let `li = gltf::nodes[a.nodes.first + P[o] as int].light`, `rgb = float3 { P[o + 1], P[o + 2], P[o + 3] }`; set `gltf::plights[li].rgb = rgb`; when `gltf::plights[li].kind != 0 && j >= 0` set `s3d::lights[j].rgb = rgb`, set `s3d::lights[j].range = linalg::f(sqrt((max(rgb.x, max(rgb.y, rgb.z)) * 1000.0) as real))` and add 1 to `j`.

`fn capture()`: with `w = C[29] as int` and `h = C[30] as int`, set `C[28] = 0.0`; set `s3d::look.ao_samples = 70` and `s3d::gtao_steps = 17`; call `s3d::init(w, h)`; set `s3d::temporal_reset = true`; `let target = gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`; run `s3d::render(target)` followed by `gfx::flush()` `C[38] as int` times, so each sample reaches the GPU as its own submission; `gfx::save_png(target, "/out/render.png")` (ignore the bool with `let saved =`); `gfx::release(target)`; set `s3d::look.ao_samples = 32` and `s3d::gtao_steps = 8`; `s3d::init(iw, ih, sw, sh)`.

`export fn hr_stop()` only calls `web::frames(false)`.

`export fn he_frame(t real)`: return if `gfx::frame()` is false. Call `apply_view()`, `apply_light()` and `apply_pose()`. When `C[28] > 0.5` call `capture()` and return. Let `z = gfx::screen_size()`, `k = if C[39] > 0.0 { C[39] } else { 1.0 }`, `rw = max((z.x * k) as int, 1)` and `rh = max((z.y * k) as int, 1)`; when `z.x as int != sw`, `z.y as int != sh`, `rw != iw` or `rh != ih`, update sw, sh, iw and ih and call `s3d::init(iw, ih, sw, sh)`. Finally, when `s3d::render_begin()` is true, call `s3d::render_end(gfx::screen())`.
